 4. 🍸 1 for the road: Union Station&#x27;s glam new bar 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Albert Ting/Continental Club A fancy new cocktail bar just pulled into Washington's Union Station, Axios D.C.'s Anna Spiegel reports. 

 Continental Club, a lofty cocktail lounge at the station's soaring Beaux-Arts Main Hall, opens today through the end of the year. 🚂 Founder Rochelle Julich tells Axios that the narrow rooms overlooking the station reminded her of train cars, inspiring a look modeled after vintage parlor cars and refreshments that nod to the "Golden Age of Rail."

 Think mahogany, brass and blue velvet, with Union Station's gilded architecture and historic Legionnaire statues as the backdrop. Photo: Albert Ting/Continental Club 🥃 The drink menu riffs on Prohibition-era classics like Bee's Knees and Manhattans, alongside modern spins like a cucumber-basil Capitol Gimlet.

 Bar bites include fried chicken biscuit bites, truffle popcorn and "railway style" hot dogs with mustard, relish and onions. Go deeper ... Get Axios Local . 

 
 
